+# AUDIT REPORT 20261008-052932 (PRE-audit, plan review)
+PATCH: N/A (PRE-audit of implementation plan for issue #276; no code diff exists yet)
+FILES: userspace/xmodem.c (NEW, planned), userspace/xmodem_crc.h (NEW, planned), src/kernel/test/test_lib.cpp (EXTEND +2 CRC tests, planned), docs/specs/xmodem.md (NEW, planned), tools/xmodem_send.py (NEW, planned), tools/verify-276.exp (NEW, planned)
+
+## FINDINGS
+- [S3] userspace/xmodem.c (planned base64/hex framing decoders) — per-framing decode-output clamp unstated
+  WHY: Three framings share one receive core over a 1 kB static window plus 512 B staging, so each decoder needs an explicit fail-closed bound (decoded bytes <= window cap, overlong line rejected) to keep the static-only sizing claim structural rather than assumed.
+- [S3] userspace/xmodem_crc.h (planned CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE) — 16-bit accumulator masking unstated
+  WHY: C promotes unsigned short to int through the shift/xor loop, so masking the accumulator to 0xFFFF on shift/finalize keeps the "123456789"->0x31C3 self-test vector portable beyond the x86_64-elf 16-bit-short target the plan builds for.
+
+DECISION: APPROVED
